# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY drift oracle for the SPRING-BFF archetype.
#
# EXEMPLAR MEMBER = snapdragon-admin-bff-api (the Phase-3 seed). These are the
# ORIGINAL literal token values the archetype recipe carries in the READ-ONLY
# upstream base. NOT secrets, NOT tenant brand — the base's own identity.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders each recipe anchor's find AND replace
# with EXACTLY these values and asserts, per anchor:
#   (1) find@upstream still occurs in the freshly-pulled base  (anchor still bites)
#   (2) replace@upstream == find@upstream                      (round-trip no-op)
# A base that drifts the anchored region (moved/renamed the seam) breaks (1) and
# the validator fails loudly. This is the anchored-region compare that replaces
# the Phase-3 whole-file byte-compare (a 2nd BFF's file legitimately differs from
# the exemplar, so only the recipe-touched hunks are asserted).
#
# NOT consumed at emit time — render-tenant-set.sh derives REAL tenant values from
# the brand profile + the repos[] identity row. Drift oracle only.
#
# Shell-sourced KEY=VALUE (same idiom as brands/*.conf).
CLUSTER_DOMAIN="snapdragon.systems"
BRAND_TITLE="Snapdragon"
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="Snapdragon-Systems/snapdragon-generator"
